# playpick cell: mode=walk boss=host spec=druid:guardian style=good
# size=10 difficulty=normal view=844x390,touch save=fresh. boss=host (The
# Reeking Host) is a coverage label only -- direction.md's [[#6]] has said
# this every time a mode=walk cell shows up: `evening` steers at no boss, so
# this starts at the door same as any other 10-normal evening and whatever
# room it reaches is whatever it reaches.
#
# Checked sessions.jsonl first (grep for druid:guardian, 7 prior appearances):
# this spec has been played in mode=clear (wander, flee), mode=battleground
# (mash x2), mode=raid (idle) and mode=walk (good, but only at carried/
# 25-heroic/820x1180). `good`-style evening on this spec at 10-normal/fresh
# has never run, and no druid:guardian session of any kind has used an
# 844x390 landscape touch viewport -- every prior touch reading for this
# spec was portrait (390x844 or 820x1180).
#
# Why the spec matters for [[#6]]/#271 specifically: every style that has
# crossed THE VIGIL clean or wiped there so far was read as a DPS or healer
# body reacting to hazards/distance. `good`'s own steering (scripts/playbot.ts)
# computes threat/positioning generically, but a guardian druid is the
# roster's tank -- taunt range and threat-holding behaviour inside a corridor
# full of watchmen (not a boss room) has not been exercised by this line at
# all yet, since every prior #271 confirmation used a dps or healer spec. If
# the tank's own aggro-holding changes how many watchmen the party is fighting
# at once mid-crossing, that would be a genuinely new variable in a stall this
# well-confirmed already, not a twentieth repeat of the same shape.
open
targets
shot front

tap raid
shot raid-setup
tap next
tap class:druid:guardian
shot class-selected
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot arrive-threshold

evening good 220 6
state
bill
shot end
says
